ring refused.\nBefore Watts, J., Marion, November, 1909.\nAffirmed.\nAction by Bank of Marion against Southern Express Co. From judgment for plaintiff, defendant appeals.\nMessrs. Willcox & Willcox, James W. Johnson, and Henry B. Davis, for appellant. Messrs. Willcox & Will-cox, and Henry B. Davis,\ncite: Carrier is not liable zvhere it shows impossibility of loss on its line: 101 Am. St. R., 398; 94 Am, St. R., 656; 30 Am. St. R.\u201e 577; 4 Ell, on R. R\u201e sec. 1450; 3 Hutch, uni Car., sec. 1347.\nMessrs. Mullins & Hughes, and W. C. Woods, contra.\nThe opinion in this case -was filed July 18, 1910, but held up on petition for rehearing until\nAugust 8, 1910."}, "file_name": "0533-01", "first_page_order": 543, "last_page_order": 544}